Yes. The strongest ETHOnline build is **not “make Moltwork more blockchainy.”** It is: take the WorkerKit execution/evidence loop you already have and make a run independently verifiable, economically settleable, and safely delegatable using existing standards. Your current repo is already unusually well-shaped for this because the append-only ledger, run lifecycle, verification gate, cost model, and receipt abstraction already exist.

One important constraint first: ETHGlobal’s Classic track prohibits pre-existing project-specific work, while Continuity tracks explicitly permit extending an existing codebase if you disclose the baseline and build substantive new functionality during the event. For `prx0r/mw`, **Continuity / Extend Open Source is the natural route**. Do architecture/research now; preserve the cryptographic integration itself as hackathon-period work. ([ETHGlobal][1])

# MOLTWORK ETHONLINE 2026 — CRYPTOGRAPHIC WORK PROTOCOL DEVELOPMENT PLAN

## 0. The hackathon project in one sentence

**Moltwork lets an autonomous agent accept paid work, execute it inside a verifiable TEE, produce a cryptographically bound execution receipt, settle the job through standard Ethereum commerce primitives, and optionally lease narrowly scoped agent capabilities without revealing the agent's secrets.**

The flow is:

```text
Opportunity
     ↓
WorkerKit economic decision
     ↓
ERC-8183 funded job
     ↓
ERC-7710 capability delegation
     ↓
Phala/dstack TEE
     ↓
WorkerKit execution
     ↓
append-only event chain
     ↓
artifact + cost + outcome commitments
     ↓
TEE-derived signature
     ↓
fresh remote attestation
     ↓
independent verifier
     ↓
ERC-8004 validation/reputation
     ↓
ERC-8183 completion + settlement
     ↓
Moltwork labor graph / marketplace
```

That gives us a real primitive:

> **Verifiable autonomous work.**

And later:

> **Leaseable verifiable autonomous workers.**

