# 1. Do not rewrite WorkerKit

The existing WorkerKit already has most of the non-chain semantics we want.

Its current lifecycle is approximately:

```text
WorkOrder
  ↓
WorkerRun
  ↓
WorkerEvent[]
  ↓
CostEvent[]
  ↓
Artifact
  ↓
VerificationResult
  ↓
CommitDecision
  ↓
SubmissionReceipt
  ↓
OutcomeReceipt
  ↓
SettlementReceipt
```

The event store is append-only and hashes every event against the previous event for that run.

And `WorkerKit.close()` already computes the chain head and places it into a `WorkReceipt`.

**That is exactly where the crypto boundary should go.**

Current:

```text
WorkerKit.close()
      ↓
WorkReceipt
      ↓
JSON file
```

ETHOnline version:

```text
WorkerKit.close()
      ↓
canonical run commitment
      ↓
TEE-derived signature
      ↓
dstack Attestation
      ↓
AttestedWorkReceiptV1
      ↓
independent verifier
      ↓
on-chain evidence
```

Do not make blockchain calls permeate WorkerKit.

WorkerKit should remain capable of running completely off-chain.

