# 2. There is one important deficiency in the current receipt

Your existing `WorkReceipt` is a good prototype, but it isn't yet a serious cryptographic receipt.

Right now its root commits to roughly:

```text
work_order_id
events_hash
known_cost
status
number_of_outputs
```

and emits an in-toto-shaped statement.

It does **not** yet cryptographically bind:

```text
actual artifact hashes
worker manifest
agent identity
execution policy
container/image identity
TEE identity
job contract
job ID
delegation
payment references
model configuration
input commitment
receipt signer
attestation freshness
```

Also, `worker_id` is currently populated from `run.work_order_id`, which is semantically wrong even if it doesn't currently break anything.

So don't mutate `WorkReceipt` into an enormous object.

Add a new layer:

```text
WorkReceipt
     ↓
AttestedWorkReceiptV1
```

