# 36. Threat model — write this before implementing

Your `THREATMODEL.md` should explicitly enumerate:

### Infrastructure operator

Threat:

```text
host modifies worker
host reads secrets
host fabricates run
```

Defense:

```text
TEE isolation
measured workload
remote attestation
```

### Mutable deployment

Threat:

```text
registry serves malicious "latest" image
```

Defense:

```text
digest-pinned images
compose hash verification
```

### Attestation replay

Threat:

```text
old valid quote reused
```

Defense:

```text
fresh verifier nonce bound into reportData
```

### Receipt substitution

Threat:

```text
valid quote attached to different run
```

Defense:

```text
receiptDigest bound into reportData
```

### Malicious renter

Threat:

```text
renter drains agent wallet
```

Defense:

```text
ERC-7710 caveats
allowed target
allowed methods
spend cap
expiry
```

### Compromised worker

Threat:

```text
agent runtime attempts unauthorized transaction
```

Defense:

```text
onchain delegation caveats still enforce policy
```

### Malicious model provider

If you're calling OpenAI/Anthropic/etc. externally from inside the TEE:

```text
TEE DOES NOT make the external inference provider confidential.
```

The provider can still see whatever request you send to them.

Be explicit about that.

### Malicious WorkerKit application

Attestation proves:

> this was the expected code.

It does **not** prove:

> this code was logically correct.

dstack itself distinguishes code identity from application correctness. ([GitHub][9])

### Secret leakage through logs

Never include:

```text
API keys
wallet secrets
private prompts
raw credentials
sensitive memory
```

in attested public receipts.

Commit to them if required.

Do not reveal them.

