# 37. Test suite

## Receipt invariants

```text
same run → same canonical digest
changed artifact → different digest
changed policy → different digest
changed chain head → different digest
changed job → different digest
```

## Ledger invariants

You already have these conceptually:

```text
modify event → chain invalid
delete middle event → chain invalid
change previous hash → invalid
empty chain → invalid
```

## TEE invariants

```text
wrong compose hash → reject
wrong workload measurement → reject
bad signature → reject
wrong receipt digest → reject
stale challenge → reject
replayed attestation → reject
untrusted signing key → reject
```

## Delegation invariants

```text
allowed target → succeeds
unapproved target → reverts

allowed selector → succeeds
unapproved selector → reverts

$2 spend under $5 limit → succeeds
$10 spend → reverts

before expiry → succeeds
after expiry → reverts

revoked lease → reverts
```

## ERC-8183 invariants

```text
cannot submit before funded
wrong provider cannot submit
cannot complete before submission
wrong evaluator cannot complete
completion releases expected funds
expired job refunds according to protocol
receipt hash preserved
```

## End-to-end invariant

One command should eventually prove:

```text
create job
fund job
delegate authority
run worker in TEE
generate artifact
close WorkerKit run
sign receipt
create attestation
independently verify
submit job
complete job
settle funds
write outcome
update agent evidence
verify entire WorkerKit chain
```

That is your golden test.

